DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions  calculate  the  complex  arc cosine of _z.  If _y _= _c_a_‐
       _c_o_s_(_z_), then _z _= _c_c_o_s_(_y_).  The real part of _y is chosen in the interval
       [0,pi].

       One has:

           cacos(z) = -i * clog(z + i * csqrt(1 - z * z))

